53a7b02ffevt2pyzyVSSHZci\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_nsv5CTSVfJ0RLG25ExBWzFNj\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation_rules.md\",\"offset\":60,\"limit\":20},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation_rules.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n60: | `FOLDER_NAMING`      | ERROR    | Folder path   | Folder follows ###-short-name convention       |\\n61: | `FRONTMATTER_VALID`  | ERROR    | spec docs     | YAML frontmatter properly structured           |\\n62: | `COMPLEXITY_MATCH`   | WARNING  | All levels    | Content metrics match declared level           |\\n63: | `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\\n64: | `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\\n65: | `SECTION_COUNTS`     | WARNING  | All levels    | Section counts within expected ranges          |\\n66: | `PHASE_LINKS`        | WARNING  | Phased specs  | Parent-child phase references valid            |\\n67: | `PHASE_PARENT_CONTENT` | WARNING | Phase parents | Phase-parent `spec.md` avoids consolidation/migration narratives |\\n68: | `CURRENT_STATE_DISCIPLINE` | INFO | implementation summaries | Long-lived summaries avoid migration-history narratives |\\n69: \\n70: > **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set (37 rules including FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK, TOC_POLICY, SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY, TEMPLATE_HEADERS, SECTION_COUNTS, and strict-only validators) and their canonical severities live in [`scripts/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../scripts/lib/validator-registry.json).\\n71: \\n72: ### Non-Breaking Acceptance Coverage Rollout\\n73: \\n74: `AC_COVERAGE` is intentionally registered at INFO severity and stays disabled unless `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=true`. This preserves existing strict-validation outcomes while making the coverage signal available to operators who opt in. The current rule is advisory: it reports the coverage denominator, covered count, configured floor, manual-infeasible escape hatch status, and malformed evidence citations without adding strict warnings or errors. The `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE` flag is documented as a future promotion switch; changing validation outcome requires a later severity change backed by adoption evidence.\\n75: \\n76: **Rule ID:** `AC_COVERAGE`  \\n77: **Severity:** INFO  \\n78: **Default:** Disabled. Set `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=true` to run the advisory scan.  \\n79: **Lifecycle predicate:** Level 2+ only, with `checklist.md` present and `implementation-summary.md` status in-progress or later. Level 1 folders and fresh scaffolds are exempt.  \\n\\n(Showing lines 60-79 of 1108. Use offset=80 to continue.)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"| `FOLDER_NAMING`      | ERROR    | Folder path   | Folder follows ###-short-name convention       |\\n| `FRONTMATTER_VALID`  | ERROR    | spec docs     | YAML frontmatter properly structured           |\\n| `COMPLEXITY_MATCH`   | WARNING  | All levels    | Content metrics match declared level           |\\n| `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\\n| `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\\n| `SECTION_COUNTS`     | WARNING  | All levels    | Section counts within expected ranges          |\\n| `PHASE_LINKS`        | WARNING  | Phased specs  | Parent-child phase references valid            |\\n| `PHASE_PARENT_CONTENT` | WARNING | Phase parents | Phase-parent `spec.md` avoids consolidation/migration narratives |\\n| `CURRENT_STATE_DISCIPLINE` | INFO | implementation summaries | Long-lived summaries avoid migration-history narratives |\\n\\n> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set (37 rules including FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK, TOC_POLICY, SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY, TEMPLATE_HEADERS, SECTION_COUNTS, and strict-only validators) and their canonical severities live in [`scripts/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../scripts/lib/validator-registry.json).\\n\\n### Non-Breaking Acceptance Coverage Rollout\\n\\n`AC_COVERAGE` is intentionally registered at INFO severity and stays disabled unless `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=true`. This preserves existing strict-validation outcomes while making the coverage signal available to operators who opt in. The current rule is advisory: it reports the coverage denominator, covered count, configured floor, manual-infeasible escape hatch status, and malformed evidence citations without adding strict warnings or errors. The `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE` flag is documented as a future promotion switch; changing validation outcome requires a later severity change backed by adoption evidence.\\n\\n**Rule ID:** `AC_COVERAGE`  \\n**Severity:** INFO  \\n**Default:** Disabled. Set `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=true` to run the advisory scan.  \\n**Lifecycle predicate:** Level 2+ only, with `checklist.md` present and `implementation-summary.md` status in-progress or later. Level 1 folders and fresh scaffolds are exempt.  \",\"truncated\":true,\"loaded\":[],\"display\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation_rules.md\",\"text\":\"| `FOLDER_NAMING`      | ERROR    | Folder path   | Folder follows ###-short-name convention       |\\n| `FRONTMATTER_VALID`  | ERROR    | spec docs     | YAML frontmatter properly structured           |\\n| `COMPLEXITY_MATCH`   | WARNING  | All levels    | Content metrics match declared level           |\\n| `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\\n| `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\\n| `SECTION_COUNTS`     | WARNING  | All levels    | Section counts within expected ranges          |\\n| `PHASE_LINKS`        | WARNING  | Phased specs  | Parent-child phase references valid            |\\n| `PHASE_PARENT_CONTENT` | WARNING | Phase parents | Phase-parent `spec.md` avoids consolidation/migration narratives |\\n| `CURRENT_STATE_DISCIPLINE` | INFO | implementation summaries | Long-lived summaries avoid migration-history narratives |\\n\\n> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set (37 rules including FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK, TOC_POLICY, SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY, TEMPLATE_HEADERS, SECTION_COUNTS, and strict-only validators) and their canonical severities live in [`scripts/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../scripts/lib/validator-registry.json).\\n\\n### Non-Breaking Acceptance Coverage Rollout\\n\\n`AC_COVERAGE` is intentionally registered at INFO severity and stays disabled unless `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=true`. This preserves existing strict-validation outcomes while making the coverage signal available to operators who opt in. The current rule is advisory: it reports the coverage denominator, covered count, configured floor, manual-infeasible escape hatch status, and malformed evidence citations without adding strict warnings or errors. The `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE` flag is documented as a future promotion switch; changing validation outcome requires a later severity change backed by adoption evidence.\\n\\n**Rule ID:** `AC_COVERAGE`  \\n**Severity:** INFO  \\n**Default:** Disabled. Set `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=true` to run the advisory scan.  \\n**Lifecycle predicate:** Level 2+ only, with `checklist.md` present and `implementation-summary.md` status in-progress or later. Level 1 folders and fresh scaffolds are exempt.  \",\"lineStart\":60,\"lineEnd\":79,\"totalLines\":1108,\"truncated\":true}},\"title\":\".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation_rules.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1781786904540,\"end\":1781786904612}},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"fc_099452138d070bb0016a33e9186414819197d2290f4a5cd419\"}},\"id\":\"prt_edac687d7001XMj6Q6XdVZvFdv\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1253a7b02ffevt2pyzyVSSHZci\",\"messageID\":\"msg_edac64d0d001Su070ZJQi25S6N\"}}\n./specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/008-template-contracts-and-acceptance-criteria/001-spec-template-context-optimization/research/lineages/pi-flash-a/iterations/iteration-002.md:38:- `check-complexity.sh:10-12` (RULE COMPLEXITY_MATCH, severity warn) validates declared level vs actual content — the Agentless \"complexity should match the task\" lesson, as a validator rule.\n./specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/008-template-contracts-and-acceptance-criteria/001-spec-template-context-optimization/research/lineages/pi-flash-a/research.md:91:`check-complexity.sh:10-12` (COMPLEXITY_MATCH, warn) validates declared level vs actual content.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:61:| `COMPLEXITY_MATCH`   | WARNING  | All levels    | Content metrics match declared level           |\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:596:## 9. COMPLEXITY_MATCH\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-validation-extended.sh:939:if begin_category \"Individual Rule: COMPLEXITY_MATCH (check-complexity.sh)\"; then\n./specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization/003-memory-and-causal-runtime/001-continuity-memory-runtime/002-fix-memory-quality/implementation-summary.md:196:- The parent `COMPLEXITY_MATCH` strict-validator warning (`Tasks (3) below minimum (4) for Level 2`) is a historical content-shape warning not targeted by any of the 22 deep-review findings; remains open.\n./specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/030-spec-kit-simplification-research/005-overengineering-simplification/research/lineages/deepseek-v4-flash-overengineering/iterations/iteration-006.md:14:- `check-level.sh` (LEVEL_DECLARED, info): explicit vs inferred declaration. `check-level-match.sh` (LEVEL_MATCH, error, 254 L): declared-level consistency across docs. `check-complexity.sh` (COMPLEXITY_MATCH, error, 207 L): declared complexity label vs content. Three checks, three different declared fields/degrees — no collapse candidate.\n./specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/030-spec-kit-simplification-research/005-overengineering-simplification/research/lineages/deepseek-v4-flash-overengineering-r3/iterations/iteration-002.md:53:- COMPLEXITY_MATCH, FOLDER_NAMING, TEMPLATE_SOURCE, TOC_POLICY, GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE headers each name distinct defect classes; no class-level overlap with a sibling beyond the family findings above.\n./specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/030-spec-kit-simplification-research/005-overengineering-simplification/research/lineages/deepseek-v4-flash-overengineering-r3/research.md:53:Verified correct (rows 13-39): the children trio (DRIFT/IDENTITY/SHAPE) is not redundant — each header names a distinct condition and the same documented writer semantics; canonical-save's five-rows-one-script shape is the census-kept F8 with per-row failure attribution still stated; acceptance pair stands; command and template-origin rules (COMPLEXITY_MATCH, FOLDER_NAMING, TEMPLATE_SOURCE, TOC_POLICY) name distinct defect classes. F3-02 resolved toward \"undocumented split\" (downgraded from duplication), and F3-01 gained the check-level-match.sh header evidence.\n./specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/030-spec-kit-simplification-research/005-overengineering-simplification/research/lineages/glm-5-3-flash-overengineering-r3-partial/iteration-002.md:7:**Row 13–39 identity:** 13 CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION, 14 POST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT (both `ts:spec-doc-structure` — no physical script, covered by it.1 F3-03), 15 TOC_POLICY, 16 AI_PROTOCOLS, 17 COMPLEXITY_MATCH, 18 FOLDER_NAMING, 19 FRONTMATTER_VALID, 20 GREP_CONVENTION, 21 LEVEL_MATCH, 22 GRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT, 23 GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT, 24 GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY, 25 GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE, 26 METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY, 27 DESCRIPTION_SHAPE, 28 NORMALIZER_LINT, 29 SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY, 30 TEMPLATE_SOURCE, 31–35 CANONICAL_SAVE_{ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED, SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED, LINEAGE_REQUIRED, PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED, DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS}, 36 CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS, 37 GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY, 38 GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT, 39 IMPROVEMENT_ARTIFACTS. Physical implementations read (headers only): 17 bash scripts + 3 `validation/*.ts` modules + LEVEL_MATCH's remainder + check-links.sh (the F2-11 standalone, read for the overlap probe). Rows 13–14: header evidence = their registry descriptions + the orchestrator's :946-948 pushes.\n./specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/030-spec-kit-simplification-research/005-overengineering-simplification/research/lineages/glm-5-3-flash-overengineering-r3-partial/iteration-002.md:57:2. Does COMPLEXITY_MATCH's body tail (:195-207) ever emit warn/fail? The five assignments observed (:123-194) are pass/info only; the head-5 grep truncated the remainder — which of its two written severities is behaviorally true is undecided (F3-05c's caveat).\n./specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/scratch/merge-041-050/final-validation.txt:560:+ COMPLEXITY_MATCH: Complexity level consistent with content (Level 2; phases=3, tasks=10, stories=0, scenarios=0)\n./specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/scratch/merge-041-050/final-validation.txt:615:+ COMPLEXITY_MATCH: Complexity level consistent with content (Level 2; phases=3, tasks=9, stories=0, scenarios=0)\n./specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/scratch/merge-041-050/final-validation.txt:718:+ COMPLEXITY_MATCH: Complexity level consistent with content (Level 2; phases=3, ta